From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mili Maintainers
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 09:15:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bootstrap Mili optimization subsystems

fun.bm.mili.MiliOptimizations.init() is the only lifecycle entry point for the
whole Mili optimization stack (MiliChunkSystem, VillagerOptimizer, RegionBalancer,
SmartRegionManager, NetworkOptimizer, TechnicalMCOptimizer, LagRemover). It had
zero call sites in the entire repository, so none of those subsystems ever ran.

This patch wires it next to the existing ConfigManager.loadConfigFiles() hook
(ordering matters: config must be populated before the `enabled` flags are read).

The hook passes org.leavesmc.leaves.plugin.MinecraftInternalPlugin.INSTANCE, the
same dummy plugin instance Leaves already uses for its internal scheduled tasks.

FORMER BLOCKER - NOW RESOLVED.

The subsystems reached from init() used to schedule through Paper's legacy
scheduler, which Folia disables at runtime (every call throws):

  - fun/bm/mili/utils/LagRemover.java            BukkitRunnable x3
      LagRemover.init() is invoked UNCONDITIONALLY, so it runs even when every
      other subsystem is disabled by config.
  - fun/bm/mili/utils/TPSTracker.java            BukkitRunnable
  - fun/bm/mili/villager/VillagerOptimizer.java  BukkitRunnable
  - fun/bm/mili/chunk/MiliChunkSystem.java       Bukkit.getScheduler()
  - fun/bm/mili/utils/AutoBackupManager.java     Bukkit.getScheduler() x2

All five were migrated to the Folia schedulers (GlobalRegionScheduler,
RegionScheduler, EntityScheduler). Migrating them was not mechanical: LagRemover
and VillagerOptimizer iterated Bukkit.getWorlds() and mutated entities from the
global scheduler, which is a region-thread-safety violation under Folia. Chunk
unloads, view-distance changes and every entity/villager mutation are now
dispatched to the scheduler of the region or entity that owns the target.

This hunk is rebased against the text as it stands after
0056-Force-disable-builtin-spark-plugin.patch, which rewrites the line that
follows it. 0001-Rebrand-to-Luminol.patch adds the line it follows.


diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/DedicatedServer.java b/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/DedicatedServer.java
index f8d0af6473aa3e32408b85a868fb807d9da510e6..0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/DedicatedServer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/dedicated/DedicatedServer.java
@@ -240,6 +240,7 @@ public class DedicatedServer extends MinecraftServer implements ServerInterface
         this.paperConfigurations.initializeWorldDefaultsConfiguration(this.registryAccess());
         // Paper end - initialize global and world-defaults configuration
         me.earthme.luminol.config.ConfigManager.loadConfigFiles(); // Luminol - load config file
+        fun.bm.mili.MiliOptimizations.init(org.leavesmc.leaves.plugin.MinecraftInternalPlugin.INSTANCE); // Mili - bootstrap optimization subsystems
         if (false) this.server.spark.enableEarlyIfRequested(); // Paper - spark // Luminol - Force disable builtin spark
         // Paper start - fix converting txt to json file; convert old users earlier after PlayerList creation but before file load/save
         if (this.convertOldUsers()) {
